{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And he fled and went outside.</b> It does not say 'and he fled outside,' because one who runs through the city streets — the world senses in him why he is running and what he is running for. Therefore he did not run in flight but within the house itself, and when he went out through the doorway he went out in his normal manner without running. And our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded (Tanhuma 9): ״הַיָּם רָאָה וַיָּנֹס״ (Psalms 114:3) — what did it see? It saw the ark of Joseph, concerning whom it is written ״וַיָּנָס וַיֵּצֵא הַחוּצָה״. For our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Ketubot 30a): even though the four death penalties of the court were nullified, the judgment of the four deaths was not nullified — one who was liable to strangulation either drowns in a river or dies by serunchei. And it is known that one who lies with a married woman — his death is by strangulation, and for this reason the generation of the Flood was punished by drowning in water on account of licentiousness. And it is written (Psalms 32:6) ״עַל זֹאת יִתְפַּלֵּל כָּל חָסִיד אֵלֶיךָ לְעֵת מְצֹא״ — our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Berakhot 8a) this refers to a woman, and adjacent to it is written ״רַק לְשֵׁטֶף מַיִם רַבִּים אֵלָיו לֹא יַגִּיעוּ״. Therefore Joseph, who was fenced off from forbidden relations, as it is written ״וַיָּנָס וַיֵּצֵא הַחוּצָה״, was worthy to save Israel from the flood of the waters of the sea. And this is what it says ״הַיָּם רָאָה וַיָּנֹס״ — that it saw the flight of Joseph from before his master's wife; therefore it is fitting that the waters of the sea should not overwhelm the ark of Joseph. And along the way, all who carried the ark were saved, and all Israel who went after the ark, and the Egyptians, steeped in lewdness, drowned." "And it is possible that the statement 'and he fled outside' means outside his own palace, on the model of ״וַיּוֹצֵא אוֹתוֹ הַחוּצָה״ said of Abraham (Genesis 15:5) — so too Joseph went outside the arena, to the point that there was no longer any power in the hand of the arena to dominate him; and on the contrary, he dominated over the natural forces and they fled at his voice. And this is the splitting of the Sea of Reeds on account of the ark of Joseph."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:32:43.984678314Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}